      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Run `code/main.py`. POST an `initialize` from `curl` and observe the `Mcp-Session-Id` response header. POST a second request echoing the header and verify session continuity.\n\n2. Add a GET handler that opens an SSE stream. Send one `notifications/progress` event every five seconds. Reconnect by re-GETing with the same session id and confirm the server accepts it.\n\n3. Implement the `last-event-id` replay logic. On reconnect, replay any events generated since that id.\n\n4. Extend `Origin` validation to support a wildcard pattern (`https://*.example.com`) and confirm it accepts `https://app.example.com` but rejects `https://evil.example.com.attacker.net`.\n\n5. Take a legacy HTTP+SSE server from the official registry (there are several) and sketch the migration: what changes in endpoint handling, session id generation, and header semantics."
      ]
    }
